    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Trust and love are two peculiarities of the human nature that influence our social and interpersonal relationships. This paper is a literature review and synthesis of philosophies that considers what each phenomenon is, how they develop independently of one another, how they interact, and how trust and love may change over the course of a relationship. Considering love, the particular partnership type of consideration in this paper is romantic relationships. The purpose is to educate the current generation on how trust and love influence social and romantic interaction while also providing an exploration into the concepts themselves. Through this exploration, the paper also considers the implications of the expression in trust and love for members of the current generation, one that has been cultivated in an age of ever-present technology.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
